// Correlation on a DEPTH-3 nested injected field, `__drupe.session.id`.
//
// A Read is permitted only if there was formerly a Login in the same
// session — the past Login's `__drupe.session.id` must equal the
// current Read's, referenced via `context.__drupe.session.id`. The
// sibling `region` is left as a wildcard (omitted), so only the `id`
// segment participates in the correlation.
//
// Positive/negative control across two traces:
//   trace_1: prior Login shares the Read's session id → permitted.
//   trace_2: IDENTICAL except the prior Login's session id differs → the
//            depth-3 correlation fails → NOT permitted.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{
        input.user: context.input.user,
        __drupe.session.id: context.__drupe.session.id
    }
};
